# relay.target - OS-016: the Meta OS crew target.
#
# Grouping: reaching this target pulls the crew units the OS-016
# wording names: dashboard, bus, jobs, overseer (timer; the
# service itself is symlinked into relay.target.wants by the
# image builds), watchdog, brief, and the ready gate, plus
# metaos-firstboot (which itself is wanted by multi-user.target
# and runs only while no secrets env exists yet), plus the
# watchman (OS-118), grouped here with the same standing as
# the other units, plus the gateway daemon (OS-059), which
# joins the target only once its bake lands (OS-058
# deliberately deferred it; OS-059 wires it in), plus the
# memory service ensure step (OS-078), a oneshot that
# guarantees the memory store namespaces exist at boot.
# The watchman is deliberately NOT in the
# ready gate's checked set: the gate checks dashboard and
# watchdog always (plus the secrets-gated units once secrets
# exist), and the watchman's health is the watchdog's OS-122
# crew-dark beat, not a gate line; adding it to the gate is
# owed follow-up, not silently present.
#
# Workers are grouped differently on purpose: relay-worker@.service
# is a template, so no bare template is wanted here. Instances
# are enabled per nick explicitly (OS-017), never auto-enabled,
# until the handler program and the mos.py DM-secret env path
# land. That exclusion is stated in the OS-016 record, not hidden.
[Unit]
Description=Meta OS crew target (relay.target, OS-016)
Documentation=file:/opt/relay/README.md
Wants=multi-user.target
After=multi-user.target network-online.target
Wants=metaos-firstboot.service
Wants=relay-dashboard.service relay-bus.service relay-jobs.service relay-overseer.timer relay-ready.service
Wants=relay-watchdog.service relay-brief.service relay-watchman.service relay-uplink.service relay-mcp-gateway.service relay-memory.service
